{% comment %}
  Renders the oversize package fee notice as icon rows.

  SOURCE OF TRUTH
  ---------------
  Every value comes from SHOP METAFIELDS in the `custom` namespace - the same
  values the Evenflo Custom Functions cart transform charges on. They are
  edited in that app, not in theme settings.

  This matters: the theme previously read its own `settings.oversize_*`
  values, which were a separate switch from the app's. Theme on + app off
  meant the page advertised a fee that was never charged. Do not reintroduce
  a theme setting for these - if the theme and the app disagree, the customer
  is misled.

    shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_enabled    boolean  master on/off
    shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_threshold  integer  carton size cutoff
    shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_amount     decimal  fee in USD
    shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_test_mode  boolean  tagged products only
    variant.metafields.custom.carton_size          integer  ON THE VARIANT

  Carton size is per VARIANT and populated on only a subset of them, so this
  is evaluated per variant, not once per product. A variant with no carton
  size is treated as NOT oversize. On the PDP, evenflo-oversize-notice.js
  keeps it current when the customer switches variant.

  Deliberately NOT gated on oversize_fee_per_item or oversize_fee_variant.
  per_item is a placeholder for an unresolved per-order/per-item decision - if
  it flips to false the fee is still charged, so gating display on it would
  hide a live charge. oversize_fee_variant is dead: the fee is no longer a
  separate fee product.

  WORDING: the Function now folds the fee into the cart line's own price
  (lineUpdate), rather than adding a separate "Oversize Handling Fee" line.
  Nothing itemises the $15 anywhere in cart or checkout, so this notice is the
  main place a customer learns about it before paying. The copy must say the
  price INCLUDES the fee - never imply a separate line item.

  Two rows:
    [truck]   Free Standard Shipping Included   <- only at/above the threshold
    [package] Includes $15 oversize handling    <- whenever the variant is oversize

  Accepts:
    - variant: {Object} the variant to test (required)
    - product: {Object} required while test mode is on, to check the QA tag
    - section_id: {String} used only to build a unique element id
    - context: {String} optional, 'cart' omits the element id so the markup
      can repeat per line item without duplicating ids

  Usage:
    {% render 'evenflo-oversize-notice', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant, product: product, section_id: section.id %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign fee_enabled = shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_enabled.value
  assign threshold = shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_threshold.value
  assign fee_amount = shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_amount.value
  assign test_mode = shop.metafields.custom.oversize_fee_test_mode.value

  # Test mode restricts the real charge to products tagged oversize-qa, so an
  # untagged product must not advertise a fee it will never be billed.
  assign passes_test_mode = true
  if test_mode == true
    assign passes_test_mode = false
    if product != blank and product.tags contains 'oversize-qa'
      assign passes_test_mode = true
    endif
  endif

  if fee_enabled == true and passes_test_mode and variant != blank
    assign carton_size = variant.metafields.custom.carton_size.value

    # nil (unpopulated metafield) must not compare as oversize; only a real
    # number counts. A nil threshold would make every variant qualify, so
    # require that too.
    if carton_size != blank and threshold != blank and carton_size >= threshold
      assign is_oversize = true

      # The locale string supplies the "$", so pass a bare number. The
      # decimal metafield reads back as "15.0"; trim a trailing ".0" so it
      # renders "$15" rather than "$15.0". A genuine "15.5" is left intact.
      assign fee_display = fee_amount | round: 2
      assign fee_whole = fee_amount | round: 0
      if fee_display == fee_whole
        assign fee_display = fee_whole
      endif

      # Compare in dollars against the free shipping threshold; variant.price
      # is in cents. This threshold stays a theme setting: it reflects the
      # store's shipping policy, not the fee the app charges.
      assign variant_price = variant.price | divided_by: 100.0
      if variant_price >= settings.oversize_free_shipping_threshold
        assign ships_free = true
      endif
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_oversize -%}
  <div
    class="evenflo-oversize-notice"
    {% unless context == 'cart' %}id="OversizeNotice-{{ section_id }}"{% endunless %}
  >
    {%- if ships_free -%}
      <span class="evenflo-oversize-notice__row">
        {{- 'evenflo-icon-truck.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        <span>{{ 'products.product.oversize_free_shipping' | t }}</span>
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="evenflo-oversize-notice__row">
      {{- 'evenflo-icon-package.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      <span>{{ 'products.product.oversize_handling_fee' | t: fee: fee_display }}</span>
    </span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
